{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 6f470379b382a9eb0579b010f7e6e69fcbe29160, all 72 supplied artifacts, client README first.\n\nThe two findings from 744a018a are addressed: Room/lane/shared git-common-dir are captured and the destination is reserved before the first await; all Rooms see one destination owner. Existing delayed-session, held-lane and token tests pass, including cross-Room and unrelated-repository cases. Schema-2 answered release journals are conservatively decoded as manual steps. Amendment 3's inherited files exactly match reviewed main.\n\nP2: Preserve the owner of the credential actually installed when making a reservation (packages/cli/src/main.ts:645, 781-785, 349). Reserving a new workspace replaces the complete owner record even before it can replace the file. Independent probe: install lane X; claim Y; fail Y's workspace at the held-lane read; release X. Release succeeds, leaves X's credential on disk, prints no manual cleanup step and deletes X's mapping. Its destination filter sees only the failed Y reservation. Keep reservation ownership separately from installed-credential ownership, with lease/Room/installation identity. A failed or superseded reservation must not erase cleanup evidence for the old installed file. Release should remove exactly its own installed credential without cancelling a newer reservation or touching another Room's replacement. Add failed-before-token, failed-install and delayed-retry regressions.\n\nP2: Handle existing schema-2 installed workspaces during upgrade (packages/cli/src/config.ts:267 and main.ts:349,781). decodeConfig changes v2 to v3 without establishing destination evidence or classifying its old nonempty-install mapping as needing manual cleanup. Independent exact schema-2-shaped fixture: installed marked credential, room-level workspaceRev/workspaceBy, no destinations and no owner.json. A fresh v7 release succeeds, keeps that file, deletes its mapping and emits no Manual local step. This is distinct from the correctly decoded old release journal. Migrate conservatively: retain old mappings as explicit cleanup evidence, report the exact manual step whenever ownership cannot be proved, and retain the unresolved duty. Do not infer ownership from a matching path or remove a later installation. Test both fresh release after upgrade and recovery of an older journal, including a newer cross-Room replacement.\n\nP2: Lock age is not evidence that its holder stopped (packages/cli/src/git.ts:136-138,158-160). withDestination allows any command to unlink a lock older than 30 seconds while the first callback is still running, and that first callback writes its next owner without checking loss of lock ownership. An independent two-process test ages the file by 31 seconds to model the expiry while the original holder remains active: process B enters and writes its newer installed owner; A then overwrites it with its older owner. The original unlock also unconditionally removes the current lock path. The test models elapsed time by mtime, rather than claiming a real 30-second filesystem stall. Use process/OS-backed exclusion with sound crash recovery, or a protocol that proves the previous holder cannot continue mutating the destination. Elapsed time alone cannot safely recover this lock. Keep an identity on any lock and never unlink a successor's lock. Add an active long-holder/process-contention regression and genuine crashed-holder recovery.\n\nArchitecture: Destination-level ownership is the right scope and git-common-dir covers linked worktrees. It must represent both work in flight and credentials already installed. Selection/landing revisions and journal identity remain unchanged. The new file lock is necessary across CLI processes, so its mutual exclusion must remain valid for the entire local mutation.\n\nSecurity: Existing signing, bearer and lease-response fences retain their tested behavior. No new live endpoint or job trust claim is made. The cleanup findings leave plaintext credential material locally and lose the means to explain or retry cleanup; they do not prove that the server accepts a token after release. Preserve secrets scanning and 0600 writes. The lock defect reopens cross-command overwrite if an active holder exceeds its age threshold.\n\nSimplification: One stable installed-owner record plus a separately fenced reservation is clearer than replacing installed identity with every attempt. Treat pre-owner migrations as explicit unresolved local steps. Keep genuinely unrelated repositories independent.\n\nValidation: npm ci with scripts disabled (352 packages); full root strict typecheck; 86 client Node and two Workers tests; 76 CLI tests; 66 MCP Node and one Workers test all pass. CLI bundle 948.8KiB, executable help and dry packing all four packages pass. All seven changed candidate artifacts read completely; the other 65 are byte-identical to reviewed E6. All inherited amendment/main files match reviewed fb2bd41. Three independent diagnostic tests pass, reproducing the two cleanup losses and aged active-lock overwrite. Saved outside the candidate at /tmp/artroom-checker-E7-diagnostics/checker-v7-review.test.ts; detached candidate is clean. No deployment or live Room/Artifacts measurement is claimed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af1e424208a2aa227151248c009ac918b5e4dd27","binding":"assigned","head":"6f470379b382a9eb0579b010f7e6e69fcbe29160","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:817b7c206d6fb5891ed1654236975a0c0d070d3a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f934a98fa8efcc34c1695fee9b59e58568876e3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b62c70f1fd34308a79454631210db1feb4e127c1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}